PATCH 397: FUN_1000_8039 + FUN_1000_7fbc whole-function base-loss -- the first two un-ported functions
of the in-mission windshield/HUD element-method subtree (the "crash-bucket").  Non-perturbed root-cause
(gdb hw-watchpoint + FIST_COOP_TICK, no code perturbation): the AZER3/CYPRUS/UKRAINE mission paint
dispatches display-list element methods via the icall vector; several are still pristine-Ghidra with raw
host-pointer derefs and crash the moment they are reached.  Earlier hypotheses (spurious op-0x2c
secondary viewport / d548 bit-0x80 / fb_seg dest / a dims-zeroing wild-writer) were all disproven with
clean data: 23ce's `d548|=0x80` is the legit phase terminator, 2b1e's fb_seg is always 0xA000 (dest is
fine; the crash is a bad SOURCE read from a mis-based record), and the "dims get zeroed" observation was
an mprotect single-step artifact.  The real defect is un-ported paint code.

asm (re_out/fist_dat_image.bin), SS=DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, GS=word[DGROUP:0x70]=0x2d74 (str-seg):
  8039: GS=[0x70]; DI=param_1=object near-off; SI=word[DS:di+0x97]; if word[DS:si]==0x1a ->
        frame-list off = word[GS:(byte[DS:si+0x19]<<1)+0x24fc] else word[GS:(word[DS:si]<<1)+0x24b4];
        scan <=3: bval=byte[GS:off]; stop when word[DS:(bval+di+0xad)]!=0; call 7fbc(bval,di).
  7fbc: DI=param_2=object; byte[DS:di+0x91/0xa5/0xa8/0xbb/0xcd..0xd4], word[DS:di+0xad] (cmpw);
        [di+0xa8]=byte[DS:(param_1>>1)+0x90f6]; uVar1=byte[DS:(param_1>>1)+0x90ee]; the sprite-anim
        state setter (calls bee2/bf3c/70c1; bf3c already patched 263).
Ghidra deref'd di/si as HOST pointers and dropped the GS segment; the +0xad reads are WORD not int.
Rebased every access to g_mem+0x1c000+near-off (GS reads to g_mem+(gs<<4)+off) with asm-exact widths.
Reached only via the mission-paint element-method dispatch; no passing verify flow reaches either fn (the
old host-ptr deref would have SEGV'd them) -> regression-safe (62 front-end flows untouched).

